WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.107 --> 00:00:02.063
♪ [intro music] ♪

00:00:05.594 --> 00:00:07.141
Give me one minute, and I'll show you

00:00:07.142 --> 00:00:10.242
how Cloud Monitoring 
can help you monitor, troubleshoot,

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:13.500
and improve your infrastructure 
and applications performance.

00:00:13.508 --> 00:00:15.856
Cloud Monitoring is a critical component

00:00:15.856 --> 00:00:18.205
of Google Cloud's observability offerings

00:00:18.206 --> 00:00:21.477
and provides visibility
across your apps and infrastructure,

00:00:21.737 --> 00:00:23.688
regardless of whether your app is running

00:00:23.688 --> 00:00:27.018
in Google Cloud, On-Premises, 
or in other clouds.

00:00:27.019 --> 00:00:29.107
It automatically captures metrics

00:00:29.107 --> 00:00:31.004
and allows you to define custom metrics

00:00:31.005 --> 00:00:34.100
unique to your application 
and business use cases.

00:00:34.101 --> 00:00:37.027
Using the Metrics Explorer
and Monitoring Query Language,

00:00:37.028 --> 00:00:39.201
you can analyze these metrics on the fly,

00:00:39.202 --> 00:00:40.673
identifying correlations,

00:00:40.674 --> 00:00:43.015
and easily add the corresponding charts

00:00:43.016 --> 00:00:44.218
to a dashboard.

00:00:44.218 --> 00:00:46.591
Cloud Monitoring provides 
a consolidated view

00:00:46.592 --> 00:00:49.895
of the health and performance 
of your apps and infrastructure,

00:00:49.896 --> 00:00:51.658
making it easy to spot anomalies

00:00:51.659 --> 00:00:54.309
using Google's data visualization tools,

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:55.985
out-of-the-box dashboards,

00:00:55.985 --> 00:00:58.733
where you can easily create
your own custom dashboards.

00:00:58.733 --> 00:01:01.453
But we know you can't sit around 
all day looking at dashboards,

00:01:01.453 --> 00:01:04.707
so Cloud Monitoring provides alerting 
where you can create policies

00:01:04.708 --> 00:01:09.396
to alert on performance metrics,
uptime, and service level objectives.

00:01:09.396 --> 00:01:11.372
Using Cloud Monitoring is simple,

00:01:11.373 --> 00:01:13.791
you can access it 
on the Google Cloud Console

00:01:13.792 --> 00:01:15.471
or using the APIs.

00:01:15.471 --> 00:01:16.899
If you're using GKE,

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.649
Monitoring is enabled
by default for your clusters.

00:01:19.649 --> 00:01:23.005
For VM, simply install
our agent to get started.

00:01:23.005 --> 00:01:24.862
For all GCP services,

00:01:24.863 --> 00:01:28.609
Cloud Monitoring is pre-configured 
to automatically collect metrics.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.442
It is free to monitor all your GCP metrics

00:01:31.443 --> 00:01:34.928
and comes with a very generous
free tier for custom metrics.

00:01:35.365 --> 00:01:38.937
This makes it easier to get started 
and affordable pricing thereafter.

00:01:39.221 --> 00:01:42.629
So next time you're looking to monitor
your applications and services,

00:01:42.629 --> 00:01:44.643
take a minute to look at Cloud Monitoring.

00:01:44.643 --> 00:01:48.392
To learn more, check out
<i>cloud.google.com/monitoring</i>.

00:01:48.583 --> 00:01:50.175
♪ [outro music] ♪

